The registry has exactly the right connectors. Before I rebuild the flow, I have one important question about SAP — there are four different SAP connectors available and they work very differently:

---

**Which SAP system do you post invoices into?**

- **A. SAP ERP / S/4HANA via BAPI** — classic SAP, transactions like `MIRO` (invoice entry) or `FB60`. This is the most common for accounts payable. Uses RFC/BAPI calls.
- **B. SAP OData** — S/4HANA or SAP Business Suite with an OData service exposed (REST-style API). Common in newer S/4HANA setups.
- **C. SAP Cloud for Customer (C4C)** — SAP's CRM/cloud product. Less common for invoice processing.
- **D. SAP Concur** — expense management / travel. Usually not for vendor invoices.
- **E. Something else** — e.g. you post via a custom SAP API, a middleware layer, or you're not sure of the technical details.

Also — one quick follow-up: **what specifically needs to happen in SAP when an invoice arrives?** For example:
- Create a new vendor invoice document (like `MIRO`/`FB60`)
- Update an existing purchase order
- Post to a specific SAP module (AP, MM, FI)
- Something else

This determines exactly which connector activity to use and what fields need to be mapped. The more specific you can be, the better the automation will work.

